<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nunavut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1999">1999</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nunavut is the largest and northernmost territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, created on 1 April 1999 from the eastern part of the Northwest Territories under the Nunavut Land Claims Agreement of 1993. Most of its roughly 40,000 people are <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inuit">Inuit</a>, and Inuktitut is an official language alongside English and French. Its capital is Iqaluit on Baffin Island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nunavut.jpg" alt="Nunavut" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kooma (original) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nunavut.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
